# s2a-core-server-wiring: what the lead applies after the wave. Until these are applied mixdog-app-server and mixdog-app-server-daemon do not compile
# (they read ConnectionInfo.window, ServerCapabilities.window_scope and Outgoing::is_host_claimant).

## 1. mixdog-app-server/src/outgoing.rs, impl Outgoing, after `pub(crate) fn claim`
    /// Whether `id` is a connection that holds a host claim now (a claim ends with its connection).
    pub(crate) fn is_host_claimant(&self, id: ConnectionId) -> bool {
        lock(&self.hosts).iter().any(|claim| claim.conn.id == id)
    }

## 2. mixdog-app-server-daemon/src/compose_domains/rows.rs, after `services.push(BlobService::new(blobs.clone(), tokens, &inputs.limits));`
    crate::server::install_param_refs(blobs.clone(), tokens, &inputs.limits);
(`install_param_refs` is the helper in the daemon's server.rs; it is pub(crate) and has no other caller.)

## 3. struct literals of ServerCapabilities that need the new field (rows file, [type_edits]):
- mixdog-app-server/src/tests/mod.rs, fn config(): `window_scope: 1,` after `remote: Default::default(),`
- mixdog-app-server-transport/tests/it/websocket.rs (the literal at the `capabilities: ServerCapabilities {` line): `window_scope: 1,`
- mixdog-remote/tests/it/lr9_origin.rs (same): `window_scope: 1,`
(the daemon's own literal in server.rs is done.)

## 4. Cargo
None: mixdog-app-server already depends on mixdog-app-protocol and mixdog-core-api; the daemon already depends on mixdog-core-domains, mixdog-store, mixdog-rt, mixdog-core-api and mixdog-app-server-transport.

## 5. SERVICE_PENDING
No name is added or removed by this task.

## 6. Closes (deferred-g2.md): s2a-core-blob-refs -> s2a-core-server-wiring: `param_refs::expand` in the server (done, before precheck and the validators) and the install in the composition (item 2).
